   "body": "**Ready for outside contributors** (steward `ext/opus-helper1`, operator decision 2026-10-30) · milestone ⚙️ M3 (board #324)\n\n**Before you start, read** (on `dev-swift`): AGENTS.md, docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, **ADR 0013** (storage tiers and its matrix, §3 conflicts, §4 offline, §7 account key), and the specs of LOT-060, LOT-061, LOT-064 (#345: reuse its account key and stores, do not re-derive them) and LOT-090.\n\n**Spec:** write `docs/lots/LOT-172-<name>.md` first, from this issue's scope and acceptance criteria. No HFR fact is involved, so no capture and no HFR-PROTOCOL subsection.\n\n**Things to watch:**\n- `NSUbiquitousKeyValueStore` is not in swift-corelibs-foundation. Keep the Apple implementation under `#if canImport(Darwin)` and test everything on `InMemorySyncedKeyValueStore`. Linux CI must stay green.\n- No new dependency. `HFRStorage` imports `HFRModels` only.\n- No secret, cookie, token or draft may ever reach a synced key. A test checks this.\n- The iCloud entitlement is out of scope (LOT-160/161).\n\n**Claim:** `/claim ext/<you>-<model>-<n>`. The first claim wins.\n\n**Routing:** Sonnet → Opus, or an Opus author with a Fable review. **Merge:** the author merges once merge-ready. This lot touches no session, cookie, token or HFR write, so a self-spawned review is enough.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
